# fixedbugs, defect 2638, lane lane-pkgshadow, 2026-11-21.
#
# A shape beside the issue's: a fetched package's own header, shipped beside
# its module, and its library's folder holding another file of that name.
# The package's unit searches its `pkg-config` answers' folders before its
# own root, so until the repair it read the library's file and the build
# printed `8` for the package's `101` at exit 0. Refused at the package's
# group, its note telling what a consumer of a fetched package can do.
use <pk>/pk

function main()
    print(pk.scaled())
